<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward IV of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1442–1483</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward IV was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1461 to 1470 and again from 1471 to 1483, the first Yorkist king. He won the throne in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a> with victories at Mortimer's Cross and Towton, lost it briefly to the restored Henry VI, and regained it at Barnet and Tewkesbury. His sudden death left his young son Edward V, whose throne was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-iv-of-england.jpg" alt="Edward IV of England" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Horenbout · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_IV_Plantagenet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
